#
# https://help.github.com/articles/dealing-with-line-endings/
#
# Text files are checked out with LF on every system (Hestia build): the jar holds some of them (COPYING, resources), so
# it comes out byte for byte the same whatever git's line-ending settings are, and Hestia can check its hash.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Linux start script should use lf
/gradlew        text eol=lf

# These are Windows script files and should use crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf
